  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening capacity for improved management of corals in trade in the Central American Caribbean.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will strengthen the capacities of authorities in Central America and the Dominican Republic to effectively manage and implement trade regulations for CITES-listed species of corals. The project will conduct face-to-face training of at least 30 lead government officials from at least 7 Central American/Caribbean countries on coral identification as part of the ROAVIS annual meeting through the use of the Guide to the Identification of Precious and Semi-Precious Corals which will be revised and translated into Spanish. The project will also complete an evaluation of coral trade in Mesoamerican countries to be presented at the ROAVIS meeting to support decision making and strategic planning processes to improve monitoring and controls of trade in species of potential concern.</narrative>
  </description>
